<p>OpenAI announced new ChatGPT advertising features on September 16, 2026. The update includes Sponsored Agents, AI assistance inside Ads Manager, natural-language campaign management through ChatGPT Work, and integrations with HubSpot and Shopify. For marketers, the bigger change is that ad creation, campaign management and post-click business actions are being connected more closely to an AI conversation.</p>
<figure class="article-image"><img src="/assets/images/blog/chatgpt-ads-sponsored-agents-hubspot-shopify-2026.svg" width="1200" height="630" alt="ChatGPT Ads workflow connecting Sponsored Agents, Ads Manager, CRM and Shopify"></figure>
<h2>What OpenAI announced</h2><p>OpenAI says advertisers can use natural-language prompts to create, update and analyze campaigns through ChatGPT with its Ads Manager plugin. Ads Manager also gets AI assistance for suggested copy and imagery based on landing-page and campaign context. Advertisers can review and edit suggestions before adding them to a campaign.</p>
<h2>What Sponsored Agents add</h2><p>Sponsored Agents are designed to let a person start a conversation with a business-sponsored agent after clicking an ad in ChatGPT. This changes the post-click experience from a simple landing-page visit toward an interactive conversation. Businesses still need to decide what the agent can answer, what systems it can access and when a human should take over.</p>
<h2>Why the HubSpot integration matters</h2><p>OpenAI says HubSpot is its first CRM partner for ChatGPT Ads. Businesses using HubSpot can connect an Ads account, create ads, track performance and follow up on leads inside HubSpot using HubSpot context. The practical value depends on how well the CRM data, lead process and advertising measurement are connected.</p>
<h2>What Shopify adds</h2><p>OpenAI says U.S.-based Shopify merchants can use a ChatGPT Ads app to connect product catalogs and measurement tools. The company says the app is planned to launch internationally in markets where ChatGPT Ads are available on September 23, 2026. Availability should be checked before planning an international rollout.</p>
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Marketing use</th><th>Key control</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sponsored Agents</td><td>Post-click business conversation</td><td>Define actions and escalation</td></tr><tr><td>AI Ads Manager</td><td>Copy and image assistance</td><td>Human review before launch</td></tr><tr><td>ChatGPT Work</td><td>Create, update and analyze campaigns</td><td>Limit account permissions</td></tr><tr><td>HubSpot</td><td>Lead follow-up and CRM context</td><td>Data access and attribution</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>How marketers should measure the new flow</h2><p>Do not measure the experience only by clicks. Track ad exposure, conversation starts, qualified leads, downstream conversion, revenue where available, and the cost of each stage. If a Sponsored Agent answers questions but does not create qualified demand, a higher conversation rate alone may not represent better business performance.</p>
<h2>Keep human review in the campaign workflow</h2><p>OpenAI says advertisers remain in control of AI-generated suggestions. Keep that boundary in your own process. Review claims, pricing, promotions, brand language, landing-page alignment and targeting before publishing. If an agent can change campaigns or act on a lead, give it only the permissions needed for that task.</p>
<h2>What this means for SEO teams</h2><p>AI-native ads can make the landing-page experience more conversational, but the underlying business information still matters. Product pages, service details, policies, pricing information and structured first-party data need to be accurate because they can support both human decisions and AI-assisted interactions. SEO and paid search measurement also need clearer separation between visibility, engagement and actual business outcomes.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Are Sponsored Agents the same as normal ChatGPT responses?</h3><p>No. OpenAI describes them as business-sponsored agents that can start a conversation after someone clicks an ad.</p><h3>Can advertisers let AI publish campaigns without review?</h3><p>The announcement describes AI assistance while keeping advertisers in control of reviewing and editing suggestions. Teams should set their own approval rules for campaign changes and external actions.</p>
